{title: Silent Night}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Silent night, Holy [C]night, [C7]All is [F]calm all is bright
[A#]Round yon [F]virgin mother and [A#]child, Holy [F]infant so tender and mild
[C]Sleep [C7]in heav[F]en[Dm]ly [F]peace, [C]sleep in [F]heavenly peace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Silent night, Holy [C]night, [C7]Shepherds [F]quake at the sight
[A#]Glories stream [F]from Heaven [A#]afar, heavenly [F]hosts sing Hallelujah
[C]Christ [C7]the Sav[F]iour [Dm]is [F]born, [C]Christ the [F]Saviour is born.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Silent night, Holy [C]night, [C7]Son of [F]God love’s pure light
[A#]Radiant beams [F]from thy holy [A#]face, With the [F]dawn of redeeming grace
[C]Je[C7]sus Lord [F]at [Dm]thy [F]birth, [C]Jesus [F]Lord at thy birth.
{end_of_verse}
